  "explicit_limitations": [
    "No zero-shot extrapolation to unseen hardware types (-37.0 pp even when specs lie inside the training range) or unfamiliar model families (-49.7 pp for cascade, -37.0 pp for graph-based); new hardware requires live or bootstrap jobs before nightly inclusion.",
    "w20 weights every job attempt equally rather than by GPU-hours (Eq. 6), reflecting numerous small jobs more than rare giant training jobs.",
    "Serving path currently omits some parallelism and scaling arguments used by offline training (Section 6 Future Work), creating potential online-offline feature skew.",
    "In-window internal evaluation previously overstated accuracy by >20 percentage points, and night-to-night w20 swings ~7 points (73.5%-80.6%), invalidating single-day 1-2 pp comparisons.",
    "Scheduler treats preference lists softly under capacity constraints (19.9% jobs / 30.0% GPU-h on #1 ranked in Aug 6-day slice); ~3% fleet compute cost reduction is an observational production estimate rather than a randomized A/B test, and the irreducible label-noise ceiling remains unmeasured.",
    "Proprietary Meta production system with no open-source code or dataset; figures reported directly from arXiv:2611.04057v1 without independent execution."
  ],
